            <div xml:id="d825">

                <pb facs="0681" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12550.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-07-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 18, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. President Carbajal has sent strict orders to all military commanders
                    throughout regions under their control not to execute prisoners under any
                    consideration. He will order that railway line over gap between Tejeria and
                    Tembladeras be repaired and that mail service be properly reestablished. He will
                    also order that Washington’s statue be replaced on its pedestal in Plaza de
                    Dinamarca as a proof of Mexican culture.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cardoso de Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
